GATEWAY LOG DELIVERY AND STREAM AUTHORIZATION

The system/firewall REST log endpoints return a bounded logs array. OPNsense
rows envelopes, OpenWrt logs envelopes and direct list responses are normalized;
plain text rows become message objects for the existing dashboard. Failed or
malformed adapter results return an opaque 502 instead of a successful empty log.
No vendor exception body or credentials are returned in that error.

OPNsense log queries POST to exactly /api/diagnostics/log/core/system and
/api/diagnostics/log/core/filter with current=1 and a bounded rowCount. The
read-only classifier permits only those two POST paths within the diagnostics
log controller. Clear actions, including clear/status or clear/searchRows
suffixes, remain blocked. This follows the upstream controller inspected on
2026-09-25:
https://github.com/opnsense/core/blob/master/src/opnsense/mvc/app/controllers/OPNsense/Diagnostics/Api/LogController.php
This source review is not acceptance against a particular firmware/hardware.

The /firewall/gateways/{id}/logs/stream endpoint uses the original authenticated
credential, user, organization, original site ceiling and gateway target as the
subscription boundary. It reloads authentication, current role, API-key scopes,
site grants/access level, gateway and active parents before each device poll and
again after the response. It uses the normal JWT/API-key validators, including
expiry, token-version changes, durable token blacklisting and per-device session
revocation. Removing the final site grant cannot widen an already-open stream
through the legacy zero-grant account policy.

The initial auth/read database session is released before streaming. Subsequent
sessions close between polls. An authorization change or unavailable check ends
the stream with an opaque named close event; a client must close its EventSource
and may reconnect through normal authentication. Data already delivered cannot
be withdrawn. Revocation does not cancel or undo device work already dispatched.

SSE rows come from the actual service logs field, with at most the requested
limit (maximum 500). Recent duplicate suppression retains at most 1000 SHA-256
row fingerprints. This is bounded best-effort polling, not a durable cursor,
complete audit archive, exactly-once subscription or evidence retention system.
A reconnect resets duplicate history and may repeat records or miss records
outside the polled page. This change does not implement authority revalidation
for every other gateway read/write or certify production hardware, HA or RTO/RPO.
